==============================================================================
3. ★ Within-host paired test (host is its own control)
==============================================================================
  28_ compared first-vs-repeat URLs across hosts. A host can only
  produce a repeat URL if it SURVIVED to be reused, so that contrast
  was contaminated. Here the comparison is WITHIN hosts that have >=2
  URLs, so selection into the multi-URL set cancels.
  hosts with >=2 URLs: 9411 ; URLs in them: 37831
  URLs per host: median=2 p90=5 max=853
  URLs with >= 7 days follow-up: 34609 (91.5% of the multi-host set)

  hosts usable for the paired test: 8552
  died-within-7d, first URL : 0.8524 (n=8552)
  died-within-7d, later URLs: 0.8475
  hosts where later < first: 475 ; later > first: 334 ; tied: 7743
  sign test p (two-sided) = 8.054e-07   [n discordant = 809]
  mean within-host difference (later - first) = -0.0049

  ★ A NEGATIVE difference means later URLs on the same host die FASTER
  than the host's first URL; positive means reused hosts are stickier.

==============================================================================
4. ★ Reconstitution rate, with the correct denominator (D2 fixed)
==============================================================================
  Denominator = EVERY removal on a host with >=2 URLs, not only those
  followed by an addition. For a window of W days, only removals with
  at least W days of follow-up can be counted, or a removal near the
  snapshot would be scored as a non-reconstitution it never had time
  to contradict.
  candidate removals (host has >=2 URLs): 29748

     W    n_used       recon         rate   median_gap
     1     29243        4325       14.79%        0.010
     3     28417        6016       21.17%        0.088
     7     27019        6736       24.93%        0.293
    30     19536        6101       31.23%        0.795

  ★ This is the displacement/resilience measure: a removal is followed
  by a new URL on the same host within W days at the rate above.
  It has no immortal-time problem because every host in the
  denominator has an OBSERVED removal.

==============================================================================
5. Falsification -- placebo removal times
==============================================================================
  real   reconstitution rate (W=7d) = 24.93%
  placebo (removal times shuffled)  = 15.76% (sd 0.19), p = 0.0000
  ★ The placebo keeps the same hosts, the same additions and the same
  number of removals, and only breaks the pairing -- so a real rate
  far above the placebo is evidence the pairing carries information.

